Known failure: range-stable — range-formatting one line of a multi-line statement adds ';' and re-indents a continuation line (#325)
A declaration keyword alone on its line (:PARAMETERS, :DECLARE) takes its
operand list from the following lines: no `;` is forced after the bare
keyword (fmt.semicolon_enforcement issue #216), including a list with a
leading-comma line from legacy code.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ChartStats;
:PARAMETERS
sChartId, aRules, nMean
, nDeviation, nLimit;
:DEFAULT sChartId, "";
:DECLARE
nIndex, nCount;
nIndex := 0;
nCount := 0;
:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ChartStats;
	:PARAMETERS
	sChartId, aRules, nMean
	, nDeviation, nLimit;
	:DEFAULT sChartId, "";
	:DECLARE
	nIndex, nCount;
	nIndex := 0;
	nCount := 0;
	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:11-3:17 hint unused_variable: Variable 'aRules' is declared but never used
3:19-3:24 hint unused_variable: Variable 'nMean' is declared but never used
4:3-4:13 hint unused_variable: Variable 'nDeviation' is declared but never used
4:15-4:21 hint unused_variable: Variable 'nLimit' is declared but never used
